message: "If you use PersonalAIty in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "PersonalAIty: an open specification for AI personality"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pinto
    given-names: Gianmarco
repository-code: "https://github.com/gianmarco-pinto/personalAIty"
url: "https://gianmarco-pinto.github.io/personalAIty/demo/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - ai
  - personality
  - persona
  - hexaco
  - psychometrics
  - llm
  - system-prompt
  - open-standard
abstract: >-
  An open, declarative format for defining the personality of an AI system
  once — HEXACO-PI-R facets, Schwartz basic values, PAD emotional dynamics,
  quirks, context modulation and hard boundaries — and rendering it
  coherently across any embodiment: chatbots, voice agents, social content,
  game NPCs. Ships with reference compilers (chat, social) and a
  psychometric adherence eval (PI-50 inventory, declared-vs-measured
  profile, sycophancy index). Spec text and persona gallery are CC-BY-4.0;
  code is MIT.
version: 0.3.1
date-released: "2026-08-14"
